  "notes": "{合|あ}う means to fit, match, or suit. It is one of the most versatile verbs in Japanese.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{合|あ}わせる→合わせる：01872_awaseru⟧ (transitive, to put together / to adjust)\n- Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧Y⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{合|あ}う\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {合|あ}って⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means \"fits / matches / is correct\" (resulting state)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦サイズ→サイズ：01363_saizu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{合|あ}う: the size fits\n- ⟦{口|くち}→口：00560_kuchi⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{合|あ}う: to suit one's taste (food)\n- ⟦{気|き}→気：02199_ki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{合|あ}う: to get along well (with someone)\n- ⟦{答|こた}え→答え：00790_kotae⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{合|あ}う: the answer is correct\n- ⟦{計算|けいさん}→計算：02697_keisan⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{合|あ}う: the numbers add up\n\nAs a suffix (〜{合|あ}う), it adds the meaning of doing something mutually:\n- {話|はな}し{合|あ}う: to discuss (talk together)\n- {助|たす}け{合|あ}う: to help each other\n- ⟦{見|み}つめ→見つめる：04571_mitsumeru⟧{合|あ}う: to gaze at each other",
